WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.710
Take «J'ai faim».

2
00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:03.670
Translate it word for word:

3
00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.180
I have hunger.

4
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.960
Try «Il fait beau».

5
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.850
Word for word: it makes beautiful.

6
00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:12.130
No English speaker talks like that.

7
00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:13.820
And «je suis allé».

8
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.610
Does that really mean: I am gone?

9
00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:19.670
So why does a word-for-word
translation from French come

10
00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.740
out as nonsense in English?

11
00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:25.350
In this mission, you'll watch a
word-for-word bridge collapse.

12
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:29.660
Then you'll drag English chips into
order for five short French phrases,

13
00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:32.090
and meet some sneaky false friends.

14
00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.230
Your mission: find out why,

15
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:37.410
and turn French into English
that people actually say.
